window.DOCS_INDEX = [{"page":"Overview","title":"Overview","href":"index.html","kind":"page","text":""},{"page":"Overview","title":"Two distributions","href":"index.html#distribution","kind":"section","text":"Two distributions Choose the deployment style that fits your project. Both distributions provide the same classes and behavior. Simple Single bundle Use dist/ui-framework.css and dist/ui-framework.js . Easy server-side i"},{"page":"Overview","title":"Framework principles","href":"index.html#principles","kind":"section","text":"Framework principles 1 ui- Conflict-safe prefix 0 0 Runtime dependencies 12 12 Grid columns A A11y Accessible interactions Included features Layout Containers, flex grid, CSS grid Forms Inputs, floating l"},{"page":"Overview","title":"Included features","href":"index.html#features","kind":"section","text":"Included features Layout Containers, flex grid, CSS grid Forms Inputs, floating labels, input groups Validation Cross-field rules, error summary, server errors Input masks Patterns, numbers, currency Selection Checkboxes"},{"page":"Getting started","title":"Getting started","href":"getting-started.html","kind":"page","text":""},{"page":"Getting started","title":"New here? Try it in 10 seconds","href":"getting-started.html#try-it","kind":"section","text":"New here? Try it in 10 seconds No server, no build step, no account. Download or clone the repository, then double-click quick-start.html in the project root to open it directly in your browser (no http:// needed — a pla"},{"page":"Getting started","title":"How it works, in plain terms","href":"getting-started.html#concepts","kind":"section","text":"How it works, in plain terms If you've never used a component library before, here's the whole mental model — there isn't more to it than this: CSS classes style things. Every class starts with ui- (e.g. ui-btn , ui-card"},{"page":"Getting started","title":"Option 1: single CSS and JavaScript","href":"getting-started.html#bundle","kind":"section","text":"Option 1: single CSS and JavaScript The easiest deployment option. Copy the complete framework folder into your static resources and include the two files, loaded after Bootstrap/CoreUI/your existing stylesheet if you ha"},{"page":"Getting started","title":"Option 2: reusable modules","href":"getting-started.html#modular","kind":"section","text":"Option 2: reusable modules Load only the component styles and scripts needed by a page. Always load tokens and core first. Copy <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/ui/static/ui-framework/src/css/00-tokens.css\"> <link rel=\"styl"},{"page":"Getting started","title":"Using alongside Bootstrap or an existing stylesheet","href":"getting-started.html#layers","kind":"section","text":"Using alongside Bootstrap or an existing stylesheet Every class is prefixed ui- , so there are no class-name collisions with Bootstrap, CoreUI, or your own CSS. The part that can collide is more basic than that: both fra"},{"page":"Getting started","title":"Server-side integration","href":"getting-started.html#server","kind":"section","text":"Server-side integration Load the framework after your existing CSS. Wrap new content in ui-scope to apply the optional base typography safely. The paths below are plain HTML — substitute your own templating syntax (JSTL'"},{"page":"Getting started","title":"Theme customization","href":"getting-started.html#theme","kind":"section","text":"Theme customization Override design tokens after the framework stylesheet. Components automatically use the new values. Copy <style> :root { --ui-primary: #143b6b; --ui-primary-hover: #0d2d55; --ui-success: #3cb371; --ui"},{"page":"Getting started","title":"Troubleshooting","href":"getting-started.html#troubleshooting","kind":"section","text":"Troubleshooting Common first-time issues, in the order you're likely to hit them. Everything looks unstyled (no colors, no spacing). The CSS file isn't loading. Open your browser's devtools → Network tab and check that u"},{"page":"Layout & grid","title":"Layout & grid","href":"layout.html","kind":"page","text":""},{"page":"Layout & grid","title":"Containers","href":"layout.html#containers","kind":"section","text":"Containers Width-constrained wrappers that center content and add side padding. ui-container-fluid is always 100% wide; the others cap out at a breakpoint and stay fluid below it. ui-container-sm (36rem) ui-container-md "},{"page":"Layout & grid","title":"12-column flex grid","href":"layout.html#flex-grid","kind":"section","text":"12-column flex grid A .ui-row wrapping any number of .ui-col-* children. Unsuffixed classes ( ui-col-6 ) apply at all widths; -sm- / -md- / -lg- apply from that breakpoint up. Every breakpoint has the full 1 – 12 range p"},{"page":"Layout & grid","title":"Explicit CSS grid","href":"layout.html#explicit-grid","kind":"section","text":"Explicit CSS grid A true 12-column CSS grid ( .ui-grid ) with .ui-span-1 – .ui-span-12 children. Unlike the flex grid, items can wrap to a new row without extra markup, and --ui-grid-columns can change the column count. "},{"page":"Layout & grid","title":"Automatic CSS grid","href":"layout.html#css-grid","kind":"section","text":"Automatic CSS grid Fills a row with as many equal-width columns as fit, each at least --ui-grid-min wide, wrapping the rest to new rows — no breakpoints to manage. Use the ui-css-grid-xs / -sm / -lg / -xl modifiers to ch"},{"page":"Layout & grid","title":"Gutters","href":"layout.html#gutters","kind":"section","text":"Gutters Use ui-g-0 through ui-g-5 on a .ui-row to control the flex grid's spacing. CSS grids (both explicit and automatic) use --ui-grid-gap instead. g-0 g-0 g-0 g-4 g-4 g-4 Copy <div class=&qu"},{"page":"Components","title":"Components","href":"components.html","kind":"page","text":""},{"page":"Components","title":"Buttons","href":"components.html#buttons","kind":"section","text":"Buttons Combine a base class with color, size, outline, pill, block, icon, and loading modifiers. Primary Secondary Success Danger Warning Info Dark Outline Ghost Pill Loading Copy <button class=\"ui-btn ui-btn-primary\">P"},{"page":"Components","title":"Typography","href":"components.html#typography","kind":"section","text":"Typography A heading scale independent of the actual <h1> – <h6> tag you use (so document outline and visual size can differ), plus a lead paragraph style, blockquote, and inline mark/code. Display 1 Display 2 Heading 1 "},{"page":"Components","title":"Form controls","href":"components.html#forms","kind":"section","text":"Form controls Text fields, selects, floating labels, validation states, input groups, ranges, and file controls. ui-is-invalid / ui-is-valid shown below are plain state classes -- add them yourself for server-rendered st"},{"page":"Components","title":"Form validation","href":"components.html#validate","kind":"section","text":"Form validation Add data-ui-validate to a form. Native constraints ( required , type , pattern , min / max ) are checked alongside cross-field rules, and messages render inline instead of in a native browser bubble which"},{"page":"Components","title":"Input masks","href":"components.html#mask","kind":"section","text":"Input masks data-ui-mask formats as the user types. Pattern masks use 9 for a digit, A for a letter and * for either; anything else is a literal the mask inserts. Numeric and currency masks group thousands for the active"},{"page":"Components","title":"Checkboxes, radios, and switches","href":"components.html#selection","kind":"section","text":"Checkboxes, radios, and switches Custom controls are label-based and coexist with global legacy checkbox rules. The label must immediately follow the input. Large success checkbox Selected radio Enable notifications Copy"},{"page":"Components","title":"Multi-select with checkboxes","href":"components.html#multiselect","kind":"section","text":"Multi-select with checkboxes Enhance a native multiple select. The original select remains in the form and receives selected values. In tags display mode, selecting more than data-max-tags (default 3) collapses the rest "},{"page":"Components","title":"Combobox","href":"components.html#combobox","kind":"section","text":"Combobox Type-ahead over a single <select> , filtering in place or querying an endpoint. The backing <select> stays in sync, so the field posts normally in a server-rendered form and validation still sees it. Parent comp"},{"page":"Components","title":"Date range","href":"components.html#date-range","kind":"section","text":"Date range A two-month calendar popover with quick presets, built over two native <input type=\"date\"> fields so the chosen range still posts with a plain HTML form. Supports full keyboard navigation (arrow keys, Home/End"},{"page":"Components","title":"Date picker","href":"components.html#date-picker","kind":"section","text":"Date picker The single-date counterpart to the date range picker: one month, one native <input type=\"date\"> , and simple Yesterday/Today/Tomorrow presets. Shares the same keyboard navigation, positioning, sizing ( ui-dat"},{"page":"Components","title":"File upload","href":"components.html#upload","kind":"section","text":"File upload A drag-and-drop friendly upload zone that lists selected files without dependencies. ⇧ Drop files here or click to browse PDF, PNG, JPG, DOCX up to 5 MB — up to 4 files Copy <div class=\"ui-upload\" data-ui-upl"},{"page":"Components","title":"Multi-step form with save &amp; next","href":"components.html#save-next","kind":"section","text":"Multi-step form with save & next A stepper wizard ( data-ui-stepper-form ) composed with the save & next toolbar ( data-ui-save-next ) on the same form. \"Next\" validates the current step before advancing; adding data-ui-"},{"page":"Components","title":"Save draft","href":"components.html#draft","kind":"section","text":"Save draft Add data-ui-draft to autosave form input to localStorage as the user types (debounced). If a draft exists next time the page loads, a banner offers to restore or discard it. The draft clears itself on submit. "},{"page":"Components","title":"Alerts and badges","href":"components.html#alerts","kind":"section","text":"Alerts and badges Use semantic color modifiers, optional icons, actions, dismiss buttons, outlines, solids, and auto-dismiss behavior. ✓ Saved successfully The record is now available. × ! Validation failed Please correc"},{"page":"Components","title":"Status lexicon and record header","href":"components.html#status","kind":"section","text":"Status lexicon and record header A fixed vocabulary for record state. The value is not the styling — it is that every screen uses the same words with the same colours, instead of each one inventing its own. Every status "},{"page":"Components","title":"Cards, list groups, and stats","href":"components.html#cards","kind":"section","text":"Cards, list groups, and stats Create panels, summary cards, action lists, and dashboard counters. Customer profile Reusable content card ✓ 128 Approved accounts First item Active item Copy <article class=\"ui-card ui-card"},{"page":"Components","title":"Charts","href":"components.html#charts","kind":"section","text":"Charts Plain SVG, no charting library. Every chart carries a generated summary label and a visually-hidden data table, so the numbers are available to screen readers and to print. Charts render in real pixel units and re"},{"page":"Components","title":"Images and avatars","href":"components.html#images","kind":"section","text":"Images and avatars Responsive images, cover/contain fitting, thumbnails, circular images, figures, hover effects, and status avatars. Rounded image with shadow Copy <img class=\"ui-img ui-img-rounded ui-img-shadow\" src=\"p"},{"page":"Components","title":"Tables","href":"components.html#tables","kind":"section","text":"Tables Responsive wrappers, borders, stripes, hover states, compact rows, sticky headers, and empty states. Site Status Action Site One Approved Open Premise Two Pending Review Copy <div class=\"ui-table-responsive\"> <tab"},{"page":"Components","title":"Smart tables","href":"components.html#data-table","kind":"section","text":"Smart tables Enhance any .ui-table with client-side search, sorting, pagination, and a page-size selector by adding data-ui-table . Mark sortable headers with data-ui-sort=\"text\"|\"number\"|\"date\" ; give a cell data-ui-sor"},{"page":"Components","title":"Table selection, columns, and export","href":"components.html#table-tools","kind":"section","text":"Table selection, columns, and export Layered onto the same data-ui-table as the smart table: row selection with bulk actions, a column-visibility menu, sticky columns and CSV export. Export covers every row matching the "},{"page":"Components","title":"Navigation and pagination","href":"components.html#navigation","kind":"section","text":"Navigation and pagination Navbar, links, breadcrumb, tabs, sidebar navigation, and pagination styles. Admin Portal Dashboard Reports Home Compliance Schedule ‹ 1 2 › Copy <nav class=\"ui-navbar\"> <a class=\"ui-navbar-brand"},{"page":"Components","title":"Tabs","href":"components.html#tabs","kind":"section","text":"Tabs Accessible tabs support mouse and arrow-key navigation. Underline (default) Profile Security Billing Profile content Security content Billing content Boxed <button class=\"ui-tab ui-active\" role=\"tab\" aria-selec"},{"page":"Components","title":"Dropdown","href":"components.html#dropdown","kind":"section","text":"Dropdown Dependency-free dropdowns close when clicking outside or pressing Escape. Actions ▾ Record actions View details Edit record Delete Copy <div class=\"ui-dropdown\"> <button class=\"ui-btn ui-btn-primary\" data-ui-dro"},{"page":"Components","title":"Accordion and collapse","href":"components.html#accordion","kind":"section","text":"Accordion and collapse Create single-open or multi-open accordion groups. General information The first panel is open. Additional details The second panel content. Copy <div class=\"ui-accordion\"> <div class=\"ui-accordion"},{"page":"Components","title":"Repeater 1.14","href":"components.html#repeater","kind":"section","text":"Repeater 1.14 A table that grows a row at a time — for \"add a row for every unlicensed premise\", \"every unregistered device\", \"every additional director\". Adding a row never touches the network: someone filling this in o"},{"page":"Components","title":"Yes / No / N-A 1.14","href":"components.html#yn","kind":"section","text":"Yes / No / N-A 1.14 Three states, not a checkbox. In a compliance or assessment checklist \"not applicable\" is a real answer and is materially different from \"not answered\" — a score excludes one and is blocked by the oth"},{"page":"Components","title":"Option cards, chips and bars 1.14","href":"components.html#option-cards","kind":"section","text":"Option cards, chips and bars 1.14 Option cards are for a choice that needs more than a label — a description, and the figures the decision is actually made on. Use the select list for long lists; use these for four or fi"},{"page":"Components","title":"Application chrome 1.15","href":"components.html#chrome","kind":"section","text":"Application chrome 1.15 The shell an internal application sits in. Every colour comes from a token, so these recolour with the theme — there is no hex value in the source. Staging environment — data here is not real. UI "},{"page":"Components","title":"Tree select","href":"components.html#tree","kind":"section","text":"Tree select A checkbox hierarchy for bulk-select trees — region → supplier → site, category → team → member, anywhere selecting a whole branch at once needs to be as easy as selecting one leaf. Checking a row cascades th"},{"page":"Components","title":"Select list 1.9","href":"components.html#select-list","kind":"section","text":"Select list 1.9 A decision layer over the tree select. The tree shows what you can pick; this shows what picking it costs . Choosing 4 of 26 regions for an inspection programme is a decision about workload, and the numbe"},{"page":"Components","title":"Filter bar 1.9","href":"components.html#filter-bar","kind":"section","text":"Filter bar 1.9 A register with four filterable dimensions rendered as chip rows takes four or five wrapped lines and pushes the table it filters below the fold — the user scrolls past the controls to reach the data, then"},{"page":"Components","title":"Register patterns 1.9","href":"components.html#register-patterns","kind":"section","text":"Register patterns 1.9 Small recurring page-level patterns that every register and workflow screen otherwise re-invents from utilities: the page header, a scope switch, a severity scale, the running summary beside a wizar"},{"page":"Components","title":"Offline work queue 1.9","href":"components.html#offline","kind":"section","text":"Offline work queue 1.9 Save draft protects the form you are looking at. This protects work you have finished but could not send — an inspector completing premise visits with no signal, an officer in a district office on "},{"page":"Components","title":"Modal","href":"components.html#modal","kind":"section","text":"Modal Small, default, large, extra-large, and fullscreen dialog sizes with focus trapping, Escape handling, and backdrop closing. Small Large (default demo) Extra-large Fullscreen ui-modal-sm × A compact dialog for a sho"},{"page":"Components","title":"Confirm dialog","href":"components.html#confirm","kind":"section","text":"Confirm dialog A promise-based confirmation modal for destructive actions, replacing window.confirm() . Reuses the modal's focus trap, Escape handling, and backdrop click. Approve application Revoke access // UI.confirm("},{"page":"Components","title":"Popovers and copy to clipboard","href":"components.html#popover","kind":"section","text":"Popovers and copy to clipboard A popover is richer than a tooltip and lighter than a modal, and can hold interactive content. Copy buttons confirm both visibly and to screen readers — a silent copy leaves people unsure t"},{"page":"Components","title":"Offcanvas","href":"components.html#offcanvas","kind":"section","text":"Offcanvas Slide a navigation or detail panel from the left or right side of the viewport. Open offcanvas Record details × Offcanvas content appears here. Status: Active Region: Central Copy <button data-ui-offcanvas-open"},{"page":"Components","title":"Tooltips","href":"components.html#tooltips","kind":"section","text":"Tooltips Use a data attribute for lightweight CSS-only tooltips. Hover me Information Copy <button class=\"ui-btn ui-btn-primary\" data-ui-tooltip=\"Save the current record\"> Hover me </button> Tooltips classes reference To"},{"page":"Components","title":"Toast notifications","href":"components.html#toast","kind":"section","text":"Toast notifications Create floating messages through the JavaScript API with configurable type, position, and duration. Success toast Error toast Bottom toast @Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' }) export class UiToast { sh"},{"page":"Components","title":"Progress, spinners, and skeletons","href":"components.html#loaders","kind":"section","text":"Progress, spinners, and skeletons Use determinate progress bars, striped animation, spinners, pulse indicators, and skeleton placeholders. <div class=\"ui-skeleton ui-skeleton-t"},{"page":"Components","title":"Empty states, stepper, and timeline","href":"components.html#empty-stepper","kind":"section","text":"Empty states, stepper, and timeline Communicate no-data states and display workflow or audit progress. 1 Details 2 Review 3 Complete ⌕ No records found Try changing the filters or create a new record. Create record 10:30"},{"page":"Components","title":"Printable document sheet","href":"components.html#document","kind":"section","text":"Printable document sheet An A4 sheet for certificates, statements and reports. On screen it is a page-like card; printed it fills the sheet, repeats the running header and footer on every page, and repeats a long table's"},{"page":"Theming","title":"Theming","href":"theming.html","kind":"page","text":""},{"page":"Theming","title":"Try it","href":"theming.html#try","kind":"section","text":"Try it These buttons rewrite a handful of custom properties on the preview below - nothing else changes. Every component inside it follows, because every component reads its colour from a token rather than from a hard-co"},{"page":"Theming","title":"Switching a theme","href":"theming.html#switch","kind":"section","text":"Switching a theme Load the core stylesheet, then a theme. Swapping the second line changes every screen in the product. Copy <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/static/ui-framework/dist/ui-framework.min.css\"> <link rel=\"styles"},{"page":"Theming","title":"The minimum worth changing","href":"theming.html#minimum","kind":"section","text":"The minimum worth changing If you touch nothing else, these five give you a coherent theme. Everything else has a sensible default. Copy :root { --ui-primary: #0b6e4f; /* buttons, links, focus rings, active nav */ --ui-p"},{"page":"Theming","title":"Token reference","href":"theming.html#tokens","kind":"section","text":"Token reference Everything a theme may set. Anything omitted falls back to the framework default. Group Tokens Where it shows Brand --ui-primary , -hover , -active , -soft , --ui-primary-100 , --ui-brand-gradient-to Butt"},{"page":"Theming","title":"Overriding without writing a theme","href":"theming.html#override","kind":"section","text":"Overriding without writing a theme Tokens cascade like any other custom property, so you can override them at any scope. This is the escape hatch for the cases a theme file is too blunt for. Adjust a theme you have loade"},{"page":"Theming","title":"Dark mode","href":"theming.html#dark","kind":"section","text":"Dark mode The framework ships a dark palette, but a theme that sets brand tokens at :root overrides it. If your theme changes the primary, it has to supply the dark variant too - otherwise a theme switch produces light-m"},{"page":"Theming","title":"Three things worth knowing before you pick colours","href":"theming.html#advice","kind":"section","text":"Three things worth knowing before you pick colours Neutrals are not neutral Give greys a cast that agrees with the primary - slate against green, warm grey against red. A true #808080 beside a strong primary is the singl"},{"page":"Theming","title":"Alongside Bootstrap or an existing stylesheet","href":"theming.html#coexist","kind":"section","text":"Alongside Bootstrap or an existing stylesheet Use the layered build so precedence is explicit instead of a specificity race. Copy <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"dist/ui-framework.layered.min.css\"> <link rel=\"stylesheet\" hr"},{"page":"Utilities","title":"Utilities","href":"utilities.html","kind":"page","text":""},{"page":"Utilities","title":"Spacing","href":"utilities.html#spacing","kind":"section","text":"Spacing Every pattern below accepts 0 through 8 (0, .25rem, .5rem, .75rem, 1rem, 1.5rem, 2rem, 3rem, 4rem), plus ui-mx-auto for horizontal centering. Pattern Property Example ui-m-* margin (all sides) ui-m-4 ui-mt-* / ui"},{"page":"Utilities","title":"Sizing & position","href":"utilities.html#sizing","kind":"section","text":"Sizing & position Class Effect ui-w-25 / ui-w-50 / ui-w-75 / ui-w-100 width: 25% / 50% / 75% / 100% ui-h-100 height: 100% ui-min-vh-100 min-height: 100vh (full viewport) ui-position-relative / -absolute / -fixed / -stick"},{"page":"Utilities","title":"Display and flex","href":"utilities.html#flex","kind":"section","text":"Display and flex Start Center item End Copy ui-d-flex ui-justify-between ui-align-center ui-gap-3 Class Effect ui-d-none / -block / -inline / -inline-block / -flex / -inline-flex / -grid the display property ui-flex-row "},{"page":"Utilities","title":"Typography and colors","href":"utilities.html#text","kind":"section","text":"Typography and colors Primary bold Success uppercase Muted small text Danger Warning Info Secondary White on primary Class Effect ui-text-primary / -secondary / -success / -danger / -warning / -info / <span class=\"u"},{"page":"Utilities","title":"Borders, radii, shadows, and hover effects","href":"utilities.html#effects","kind":"section","text":"Borders, radii, shadows, and hover effects Radius 1 Shadow 2 Hover lift Circle Pill Hover scale Class Effect ui-border / ui-border-0 add / remove a 1px border ui-rounded-0 – ui-rounded-4 , -circle , -pill border-radius s"},{"page":"Utilities","title":"Visibility and misc","href":"utilities.html#visibility","kind":"section","text":"Visibility and misc Class Effect ui-visible / ui-invisible visibility (keeps layout space, unlike ui-d-none ) ui-opacity-25 / -50 / -75 / -100 opacity ui-sr-only visually hidden but present for screen readers ui-focusabl"},{"page":"JavaScript API","title":"JavaScript API","href":"javascript.html","kind":"page","text":""},{"page":"JavaScript API","title":"Initialization","href":"javascript.html#initialization","kind":"section","text":"Initialization The bundle automatically initializes components at DOM ready. Initialize newly inserted HTML manually: Copy UI.init(document.querySelector(\"#newContent\")); Public APIs Everything hangs off the global UI ob"},{"page":"JavaScript API","title":"Public APIs","href":"javascript.html#api","kind":"section","text":"Public APIs Everything hangs off the global UI object. Most components also work purely through data-ui-* attributes with no JavaScript calls at all — these methods are for programmatic control. API Purpose UI.init(root)"},{"page":"JavaScript API","title":"How to&hellip;","href":"javascript.html#howto","kind":"section","text":"How to… Show a toast Copy UI.toast.show({ type: \"success\", // success | danger | warning | info title: \"Saved\", message: \"The record was saved successfully.\", duration: 4000, // ms before auto-dismiss; 0 disables it posi"},{"page":"JavaScript API","title":"Custom events","href":"javascript.html#events","kind":"section","text":"Custom events Components emit bubbling, cancelable events you can listen for on the element or via delegation on document . Event Fires on detail ui:validate Form validated - {valid, errors} ui:validate:server Server err"},{"page":"JavaScript API","title":"Dynamic content","href":"javascript.html#dynamic","kind":"section","text":"Dynamic content Create an alert document.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", function () { document.getElementById(\"createDynamicAlert\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () { UI.alert.create({ target: \"#dynamicTarget\""},{"page":"Angular & SPAs","title":"Angular & SPAs","href":"angular.html","kind":"page","text":""},{"page":"Angular & SPAs","title":"Setup","href":"angular.html#setup","kind":"section","text":"Setup Three things, once per application. The bundle is a plain script that assigns window.UI , so it is loaded as a global asset rather than imported as a module. 1. Load the CSS and JS as global assets in angular.json "},{"page":"Angular & SPAs","title":"Why one line is enough","href":"angular.html#observe","kind":"section","text":"Why one line is enough UI.observe(root) watches for inserted and removed nodes and calls UI.init() and UI.destroy() on them, batched on an animation frame. That covers every way Angular puts markup on the page — @if and "},{"page":"Angular & SPAs","title":"Binding to reactive forms","href":"angular.html#forms","kind":"section","text":"Binding to reactive forms Every input-bearing component keeps the real <select> or <input> you wrote and drives it, rather than replacing it with a widget of its own. So formControlName , ngModel and [(ngModel)] bind dir"},{"page":"Angular & SPAs","title":"Options and rows that arrive late","href":"angular.html#async","kind":"section","text":"Options and rows that arrive late This is the one place the integration needs help. A component builds when its element is inserted. If the element is inserted empty and Angular fills it from an HTTP response a moment la"},{"page":"Angular & SPAs","title":"Wrapping the imperative API","href":"angular.html#services","kind":"section","text":"Wrapping the imperative API The parts of the framework you call rather than declare — confirmations, toasts, modals — are worth a thin injectable so components depend on a typed service instead of a global. There is noth"},{"page":"Angular & SPAs","title":"Scoped CSS and generated markup","href":"angular.html#css","kind":"section","text":"Scoped CSS and generated markup Angular’s emulated view encapsulation works by stamping a _ngcontent-* attribute onto the elements in a component’s template, and rewriting that component’s styles to match it. Markup the "},{"page":"Angular & SPAs","title":"TypeScript","href":"angular.html#types","kind":"section","text":"TypeScript The package ships hand-written definitions at dist/ui-framework.d.ts , declaring the global UI object and a UIFramework namespace for the option and result types. They are deliberately partial: internal fields"},{"page":"Angular & SPAs","title":"React, Vue and Svelte","href":"angular.html#others","kind":"section","text":"React, Vue and Svelte Nothing on this page is Angular-specific except the names. The framework holds no reference to any host framework; it reacts to nodes entering and leaving the document, which is a property of the DO"}];
